[statement]
A package the request's packages displace goes just before its successor
even where a package replaced later still needed it: `w` 0.20 provides
`wl` at its version, which the installed `wl` 0.19 holds, and `lab` 1,
which `lab` 2 replaces after `w` is installed, needed `so:w19`, which only
`wl` provides. apk removes `wl`, installs `w`, then upgrades `lab`. The
shape of `labwc`'s upgrade from Alpine v3.23 to v3.24.

[repository]
P:w
V:20
p:wl=20 so:w20=0

P:lab
V:2
D:so:w20

[installed]
P:wl
V:19
p:so:w19=0

P:lab
V:1
D:so:w19

[world]
lab

[request]
lab>1

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove wl 19
install w 20
upgrade lab 1 2
